All Forms of Birth Control</a><i> So much for Justice Alito's &quot;narrow&quot; opinion. Less than a day after the United States Supreme Court issued its divisive ruling on Burwell v. Hobby Lobby, it has already begun to toss aside the supposedly narrow interpretation of the decision. On Tuesday, the Supremes ordered lower courts to rehear any cases where companies had sought to deny coverage for any type of contraception, not just the specific types Hobby Lobby was opposed to.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T20:23:05-07:00","id":187609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/183891-supreme-court-term-review-merged?p=187223#post187223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://talkingpointsmemo.com/livewire/religious-groups-lgbt-hiring-hobby-lobby\" target=\"_blank\">Post-Hobby Lobby, Religious Orgs Want Exemption From LGBT Hiring Order</a><br /> <i><br /> The day after the Supreme Court's Hobby Lobby ruling, a group of religious leaders sent a letter to President Barack Obama asking that he exempt them from a forthcoming executive order that would prohibit federal contractors from discriminating against LGBT people.<br /> <br /> The letter, first reported by The Atlantic, was sent on Tuesday by 14 representatives, including the president of Gordon College, an Erie County, Pa., executive and the national faith vote director for Obama for America 2012, of the faith community. &quot;Without a robust religious exemption,&quot; they wrote, &quot;this expansion of hiring rights will come at an unreasonable cost to the common good, national unity and religious freedom.&quot;</i><br /> --------------------<br /> <br /> We all saw this one coming. Sooner than I would have thought though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The religious orgs cited there are actual not for profit religious orgs. They would have filed with or without this ruling... so that's a bit misleading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2058-nobody","name":"Nobody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T20:24:18-07:00","id":187610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/183891-supreme-court-term-review-merged?p=187320#post187320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>One FBI agent met with her seven times, trying to dissuade her from supporting jihad and suggesting that she instead commit herself to humanitarian work, court papers say. Shannon Maureen Conley, 19, was taken into custody at the Denver International Airport by the FBI as she attempted to board a plane on her way to Turkey, according to Dave Joly, an FBI spokesman. The case against Conley was not unsealed until Wednesday because of an &quot;ongoing, active investigation,&quot; when news of her arrest and alleged activities became public, according to the U.S. attorney's office in Denver. Investigators from the FBI's Joint Terrorism Task Force investigated Conley for roughly eight months before arresting her April 8, according to a federal criminal complaint filed in the Denver U.S. District Court. During that time, she repeatedly told federal agents \u2014 who identified themselves and met with her on a near-weekly basis from November to April \u2014 that she was committed to waging jihad in the Middle East.</i> 19 years old...a bit young to be so crazy and deranged.</div> </div> </div> </div>Radicalization TENDS to occur before the age of 25.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2058-nobody","name":"Nobody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T20:27:31-07:00","id":187611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/183891-supreme-court-term-review-merged?p=187274#post187274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since this seems to be rapidly turning into a general grumbling thread... There's <a href=\"http://www.denverpost.com/news/ci_26077871/fbi-arrest-colorado-teen-suspected-supporting-al-qaeda\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.<br /> <br /> See. I have no grand objection to the kid getting detained and so on, but I'm wary since the way this is written it's presented that she was arrested on charges stemming from the declaration of war back after 9/11, after jumping through several hoops. I may be completely off on that, but it's the implication I'm getting and if so it's highly disturbing.</div> </div> </div> </div>The deposition says she claimed she was going to assist in attacking &quot;legitimate targets of attack,&quot; and then listed military bases and embassies. The charge there will be conspiring to help a terrorist organization harm the United States.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2058-nobody","name":"Nobody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T20:30:33-07:00","id":187615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/183891-supreme-court-term-review-merged?p=187511#post187511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">o...but wait! There's more; <a href=\"http://m.motherjones.com/politics/2014/07/supreme-court-scotus-hobby-lobby-all-forms-contraception\" target=\"_blank\">Supreme Court Broadens Hobby Lobby Ruling to All Forms of Birth Control</a><i> So much for Justice Alito's &quot;narrow&quot; opinion. Less than a day after the United States Supreme Court issued its divisive ruling on Burwell v. Hobby Lobby, it has already begun to toss aside the supposedly narrow interpretation of the decision. On Tuesday, the Supremes ordered lower courts to rehear any cases where companies had sought to deny coverage for any type of contraception, not just the specific types Hobby Lobby was opposed to.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm confused. None of the qualifiers used to narrow the scope had to do with the TYPES of birth control. The narrowing had to do with the types of RFRA claims based on organization and what laws could or could not be objected to... not the types of birth control. The other narrowing had to do with which parts of the health care law could be challenged, such as vaccinations and blood transplants, not the types of birth control. If birth control itself was found to be the issue in the original ruling, it doesn't matter that only 2 types were explicitly called out by Hobby Lobby.<br /> <br /> Plus, the order is to rehear the cases, not to rule for or against them. That's very common in civil matters where case law can change pending or appealed cases that are still in the works. This is neither a surprise nor broadening... it's exactly how civil law works (as opposed to criminal law).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2058-nobody","name":"Nobody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T20:32:56-07:00","id":187631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/183891-supreme-court-term-review-merged?p=187364#post187364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really no. Like I said, I don't have any problem with the government stepping in to deal with a potentially dangerous person, I'm just wary that it seems like they're stretching the declaration of war to cover &quot;anybody we think might be a terrorist or other baddy&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite. This would could be tried without the AUMF. It's an open threat with intent to attack military targets overseas and aid an enemy combatant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2058-nobody","name":"Nobody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T06:42:38-07:00","id":188673,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://theusconstitution.org/text-history/2753/us-chamber-commerce-continues-its-winning-ways\" target=\"_blank\">Supreme Court continues it's business-friendly direction</a><br /> <br /> And as long as the court continues to be so business friendly, the nation as a whole will continue it slide from a people-oriented government to business-oriented government, since it really took off back in the 70s when lobbyist organizations were legitimatized, and corporate contributions were validated. In 1980, the top 1 percent controlled about 8 percent of U.S. national income. The bottom 50 percent shared about 18 percent. Today the top 1 percent share about 20 percent; the bottom 50 percent, just 12 percent. Add the fact that the middle class is disappearing and (and the percentage of those in poverty hit quite a high note in the past couple years alone)<br /> <br /> So...what to do when it seems the three branches of government can't seem to man up..?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T06:57:49-07:00","id":188677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/183891-supreme-court-term-review-merged?p=188673#post188673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...what to do when it seems the three branches of government can't man up?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is unfair. The Supreme Court is doing exactly what it's supposed to and interpreting the laws the legislature has written. As angry as I am about the direction those verdicts have taken, they are legal and proper.<br /> <br /> The burden is on us, the people, to get involved in government and to make our voices heard. Get petitions; inform people; contact your representatives to alert them to your resolve. You only get to blame your elected representative for not representing you if you've told him how you want to be represented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T11:01:43-07:00","id":188812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/183891-supreme-court-term-review-merged?p=188677#post188677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is unfair. The Supreme Court is doing exactly what it's supposed to and interpreting the laws the legislature has written. As angry as I am about the direction those verdicts have taken, they are legal and proper.</div> </div> </div> </div>Judges are considered the interpreters of Law. The Supreme Court, interpreters of Constitutional Law. Sometimes that interpretation is <b>wrong</b>.<br /> <br /> For example, no amount of words being thrown around will ever convince the majority of the country that corporations are entitled to have the same rights as the individual. And yet, the Supreme Court argues for business in that.<br /> <br /> To support that outrage and why that won't ever change;<br /> From wiki; <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buckley_v._Valeo\" target=\"_blank\">Buckley v. Valeo</a>, 424 U.S. 1 (1976), <i>was a case in which a majority of the Supreme Court of the United States struck down several provisions in the 1974 Amendment to the Federal Election Campaign Act, a law that limited campaign expenditures, independent expenditures by individuals and groups, and expenditures by a candidate from personal funds. It introduced the idea that money counts as speech, and eliminated any previous restraints on unlimited spending in US election campaigns. The Court upheld the provision which sets limits on individuals' campaign contributions.<br /> A minority of the court (White, Blackmun, and Marshall) would not have held any part of the Act unconstitutional. The case was significant because it opened a chain of decisions, including Citizens United v. FEC, which allowed people with more monetary support to become more politically influential. <b>This set the United States at odds with the practice in the rest of the democratic world, particularly in Europe (see Bowman v. United Kingdom[1]), Latin America and the Commonwealth (see Harper v. Canada (Attorney General)[2]) where rules designed to limit spending at elections are common, and used to prevent conflicts of interest and to promote political equality</b></i>.<br /> ----------------------<br /> <br /> As long as money continues to rule the country, it will be in the interest of every branch of the government to keep it that way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/183891-supreme-court-term-review-merged?p=188677#post188677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The burden is on us, the people, to get involved in government and to make our voices heard. Get petitions; inform people; contact your representatives to alert them to your resolve. You only get to blame your elected representative for not representing you if you've told him how you want to be represented.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hate to break it to you, that rarely works now. A billionaire has far more say in government that Joe Average protesting with the remnant of the Occupy Movement. <a href=\"http://www.washingtonpost.com/blogs/monkey-cage/wp/2014/04/08/rich-people-rule/\" target=\"_blank\">Rich People Rule</a><br /> <br /> <i>Qualitative studies of the political role of economic elites have mostly been relegated to the margins of the field. But now, political scientists are belatedly turning more systematic attention to the political impact of wealth, and their findings should reshape how we think about American democracy.<br /> A forthcoming article in Perspectives on Politics by (my former colleague) Martin Gilens and (my sometime collaborator) Benjamin Page marks a notable step in that process. Drawing on the same extensive evidence employed by Gilens in his landmark book \u201cAffluence and Influence,\u201d Gilens and Page analyze 1,779 policy outcomes over a period of more than 20 years. They conclude that \u201ceconomic elites and organized groups representing business interests have substantial independent impacts on U.S. government policy, while mass-based interest groups and average citizens have little or no independent influence.\u201d</i><br /> -----------------------------<br /> <br /> When we vote, we vote for whatever industry to enrich.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","user":"Shadowflame","date":".  syntax 07-05-2014, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T11:43:27-07:00","id":188858,"title":"","content":"JimB had it right.<br /> <br /> If you want the kind of change you're looking for, Shadowflame, then you want a Constitutional amendment.<br /> <br /> I take it, from your non-reaction, that you also have conceded the point on the birth control post above...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2058-nobody","name":"Nobody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}